# Web files the native apps mirror by hand (docs/native/MACOS_LIQUID_GLASS_REDESIGN.md
# §A4.6): the chat request the apps send, the sidebar's rows, which drawing each
# icon concept wears, and the colour and type tokens. The generators catch a
# drifted projection; nothing else catches a field added to the chat body or a
# row moved in the sidebar. So a pull request that touches one of these carries
# the label "native: done" (the apps were updated, here or in a linked PR) or
# "native: n/a" (the change does not reach them). The `native parity` workflow
# fails without one. Make that check required in branch protection for it to
